        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"ddd2f5a8191c1ae70b57ec33\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Required: the No Service report calls for customer identification, diagnosis, applicable troubleshooting, and a justified endpoint. The setup creates several service obstacles, including a SIM lock that cannot be fixed with an available user tool.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"}],\"rationale\":\"The agent must distinguish fixable causes from the locked SIM, use device observations supplied through the user, and avoid treating setup state as information already known to the agent.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"Selected conditional endpoint: transfer is specified by the completion design and is supported by the documented locked-SIM escalation rule, but only after establishing that the issue cannot be resolved within the agent's scope.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0314\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0431\"}],\"rationale\":\"The transfer call takes a summary argument. Its main difficulty is deciding when the prerequisite for transfer has been met, rather than constructing the call.\",\"applicability\":\"selected_conditional\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":2,\"tool_use\":1,\"information\":1}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Identification, device and account diagnosis, applicable fixes and checks, and a transfer decision make this substantial multi-stage work. Setup actions themselves are not agent work.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0222\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0027\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Several simultaneous causes must be distinguished, and the agent must reconcile the instruction to attempt resolution with the specific rule to escalate a locked SIM.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0027\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The path involves selecting among customer/account tools and user-mediated device checks and fixes, binding retrieved customer and line information where needed; the final transfer call is simple.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0324\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0447\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0207\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0213\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0434\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Customer identification precedes support; device observations determine fixes and subsequent checks, while any billing-related line restoration requires payment before resumption. The unresolved SIM lock supports dependent escalation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0005\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0115\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0117\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The user supplies a symptom and phone number, not the causes. The agent must retrieve and reconcile device-reported SIM, airplane-mode and APN state with line and bill information; judge-only setup records are not agent knowledge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0003\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0006\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0222\"}]}},\"overall_score\":75,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"After appropriate diagnosis and feasible troubleshooting, transfer the still-unresolved No Service issue to a human agent and send the prescribed transfer message. The completion design specifies a no-service state, not restored signal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"The required path is not every possible telecom troubleshooting branch. Identification enables account investigation; user-grounded device checks select applicable fixes; outcomes govern whether service is restored or the locked-SIM escalation condition remains. Payment and line resumption are linked prerequisites if pursued, not independent obligations to repeat.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Ratings of 3 for workload, reasoning, tool use, dependencies, and information yield 5 × 15 = 75. The index reflects multi-cause, cross-record diagnosis and a justified escalation, not the apparent simplicity of the single reference call.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The exact diagnostic order and extent of fixable-cause troubleshooting before the locked-SIM transfer are not specified.\",\"The supplied sources do not establish how every device action updates displayed status; no execution or successful fix is assumed.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"The single native reference call omits the prerequisite identification and troubleshooting required by policy.\",\"The scenario illustrates a `get_status_bar` call, while the supplied user tool is named `check_status_bar`; this naming mismatch is not scored as task difficulty.\",\"Baseline records and device state precede the listed initialization actions and are not facts available to the agent.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
